From fd68dfd90cf61f2d99b430e9ad3b03f8062f176d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:42:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ui): build the pick overlay lines once per input

interact::selection_feature_lines outlined each shown pick again on
each scene collection. On fig8 with one welded-face pick (#2238 probe,
state c) this cost 1.48 ms per still frame in release.

The new crates/ui/src/pick_line_memo.rs keeps the lines per input: the
pick list by value, the pick ink, the vertex cross arm, and for each
picked model its display-off flag, entity, Arc<Features> allocation and
view pose. One miss runs the old build one time. The lines are display
only.

The probe now collects the scene one time before its window, as the
shell does on the first frame of an input, and asserts zero pick line
builds on still frames.

Pinned by pick_lines_build_once_per_input (each answer equals a fresh
build across a new pick, a hidden model, a move and the undos).

Fixes #2250

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
